# NestJS Backend Standards

## Modular Structure (feature-first, DDD-aligned)
```
apps/api/src/
├── attendance/
│   ├── attendance.module.ts
│   ├── attendance.controller.ts
│   ├── attendance.service.ts
│   ├── dto/clock-in.dto.ts
│   └── domain/geofence.ts        # pure domain (no NestJS/Prisma imports)
├── leave/
├── overtime/
├── user/
├── auth/
├── common/                       # filters, interceptors, decorators, guards
└── prisma/                       # PrismaService, transaction helpers
```

Domain logic (calculations, invariants) lives in `domain/*.ts` and is framework-agnostic → trivial to unit test.

## Controllers
- Thin. Only: parse DTO → call service → return DTO. No business logic, no `PrismaService` injection.
- Every route has an explicit HTTP verb, path, and response DTO type.

## Services
- All mutations that touch >1 aggregate go through `prisma.$transaction`.
- Inject `PrismaService`, other services, and domain helpers — nothing else from the request scope.
- Return domain/DTO shapes, never raw Prisma models to the controller.

## DTOs & Validation
- Every incoming payload is a class with `class-validator` decorators.
- Enable a global `ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true, transform: true })`.

```ts
// apps/api/src/attendance/dto/clock-in.dto.ts
import { IsLatitude, IsLongitude, IsNumber, IsOptional, Min } from 'class-validator';

export class ClockInDto {
  @IsLatitude() latitude!: number;
  @IsLongitude() longitude!: number;
  @IsNumber() @Min(0) accuracyMeters!: number;
  @IsOptional() note?: string;
}
```

## Guards & Decorators
- `JwtAuthGuard` → `RolesGuard` → `TenantGuard` (order matters).
- Custom decorators: `@CurrentUser()`, `@Roles(...)`, `@Tenant()`.

## Error Handling
- Throw NestJS exceptions with **stable, machine-readable codes** as messages (`'INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE'`, `'OUTSIDE_GEOFENCE'`).
- A global `AllExceptionsFilter` maps unknown errors to `500 INTERNAL_ERROR` and logs the original.

## Testing (Jest)
- Unit test every `domain/*.ts` file — pure functions, no mocks needed.
- Service tests mock `PrismaService` via `DeepMockProxy<PrismaClient>` from `jest-mock-extended`.
- Cover: shift overlap, geofence radius edge cases, leave carry-over, overtime rate tiers, approval state transitions.
